* Three layers\nfrom symptom to cause
** The symptom
*** "Cannot resolve a constrained\ntagging secret for an invalid recipient"
*** Framework assertion, not contract
*** Named none of the three real problems
** Layer 1\nthe run never started
*** zod stack overflow at deployment
*** Self-referential simulation schema
*** ^4 resolved to 4.5.4
*** Released 11 days after the framework
*** Fix: resolutions pin to 4.4.3
** Layer 2\nthe timeout
*** sleep = 3,612 s
*** timeout = 900 s
*** Could never pass, on any machine
*** Correct until the delay went 360 s -> 1 h
*** Fix: derive timeout from the delay
** The fitting wrong answer
*** Timeout killed the sleep,\nso the issuer stayed zero
*** Fitted every symptom
*** Fixing it made the deploy test pass
*** The mints still failed
** The actual cause
*** Anvil's clock does not follow wall time
*** Tip was 4.9 hours behind
*** A warp moves L1, not L2
*** An L2 block needs a transaction
*** Public view reads "now",\nprivate read reads the tip
*** Zero is not a Grumpkin point,\nso constrained delivery panics
** What generalises
*** A delayed value has a dead window after deployment
*** Constants in a relationship are written as one
*** A best-effort path hides what a guaranteed path reports
*** An unpinned transitive dependency is an unowned decision
*** A test too slow to run stops reporting
*** Waiting is not time passing
*** A fix that improves symptoms\nis not proof of the cause
*** 3,698s and 8 failures -> 142s and 0
@endmindmap
